  "conformsTo": "http://mlcommons.org/croissant/1.1",
  "name": "GQA",
  "description": "\n\n\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tLarge-scale Multi-modality Models Evaluation Suite\n\t\n\n\nAccelerating the development of large-scale multi-modality models (LMMs) with lmms-eval\n\n\ud83c\udfe0 Homepage | \ud83d\udcda Documentation | \ud83e\udd17 Huggingface Datasets\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tThis Dataset\n\t\n\nThis is a formatted version of GQA. It is used in our lmms-eval pipeline to allow for one-click evaluations of large multi-modality models.\n@inproceedings{hudson2019gqa,\n  title={Gqa: A new dataset for real-world visual reasoning and compositional\u2026 See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmms-lab-encoder/GQA.",
